## Whole-file declarations, data, registration and contextual obligations (unit-1)

This reference renders two 85x65 flex containers with unshrinkable blue items. The row nowrap container uses justify-content:start so its six items overflow toward the end; its 90px-high big item uses align-self:start. The second container actually uses column wrap despite its columnNoWrap class name, and uses align-content:start. These explicit start overrides produce the expected safe-overflow fallback for the matching test, which sets safe flex-end/center values instead. Shared styling keeps borders, sizes, floats, clearing and 100px vertical spacing equal.


